{%- comment -%}
  Seoul Glow Lab — Multi-lamp Sync
  Three rooms each holding an Apōllō Floor Lamp silhouette. Two modes:
    SYNC — every lamp glows the same scene
    ZONE — each room runs an offset scene
  Lamp SVG is the merchant-validated black-aluminium body with a continuous
  RGB diffuser channel (Brand Book v1·2026 PDP design handoff).

  Mood: Ink. Block-driven rooms (default 3) and explanation strip cards (default 3).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign room_blocks  = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'room'
  assign strip_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'strip'

  comment
  Build the cycle palette (max 6 hex stops). Keys: scene_hex_1..6.
  Empty slots fall through default to brand accents so the cycle never breaks.
  endcomment
  assign cycle_hexes = ''
  assign cycle_names = ''
  for i in (1..6)
    assign hex_key  = 'scene_hex_' | append: i
    assign name_key = 'scene_name_' | append: i
    assign hx = s[hex_key]
    assign nm = s[name_key]
    comment
      Brand-aligned chromatic flow. In ZONE mode the 3 rooms always show
      3 CONSECUTIVE entries from this list, so the cycle is ordered to
      keep every adjacent triple harmonious against the Seoul Glow Lab
      brand book trinity (purple / pink / cyan):
        1 Cyan    2 Sky    3 Indigo
        4 Purple  5 Magenta 6 Pink
      Any window of 3 falls inside the brand spectrum (cool, transitional,
      brand-grad, brand-text-grad, etc.).
    endcomment
    if hx == blank
      case i
        when 1
          assign hx = '#F2FFA0'
        when 2
          assign hx = '#38BDF8'
        when 3
          assign hx = '#6366F1'
        when 4
          assign hx = '#B0C3FA'
        when 5
          assign hx = '#D946EF'
        else
          assign hx = '#5E0A02'
      endcase
    endif
    if nm == blank
      case i
        when 1
          assign nm = 'Cyan'
        when 2
          assign nm = 'Sky'
        when 3
          assign nm = 'Indigo'
        when 4
          assign nm = 'Purple'
        when 5
          assign nm = 'Magenta'
        else
          assign nm = 'Pink'
      endcase
    endif
    if forloop.first
      assign cycle_hexes = hx
      assign cycle_names = nm
    else
      assign cycle_hexes = cycle_hexes | append: '|' | append: hx
      assign cycle_names = cycle_names | append: '|' | append: nm
    endif
  endfor
-%}

<section
  id="casa-mls-{{ section.id }}"
  class="casa-mls"
  data-cycle-hexes="{{ cycle_hexes }}"
  data-cycle-names="{{ cycle_names | escape }}"
  data-cycle-ms="{{ s.cycle_ms | default: 1300 }}"
  data-default-mode="{{ s.default_mode | default: 'sync' }}"
  style="
    --mls-paper:  {{ s.color_paper  | default: '#FAFAF7' }};
    --mls-ink:    {{ s.color_ink    | default: '#0A0A0F' }};
    --mls-purple: {{ s.color_purple | default: '#B0C3FA' }};
    --mls-pink:   {{ s.color_pink   | default: '#5E0A02' }};
    --mls-cyan:   {{ s.color_cyan   | default: '#F2FFA0' }};
    --mls-pt: {{ s.padding_top    | default: 72 }}px;
    --mls-pb: {{ s.padding_bottom | default: 72 }}px;
  "
>
  <header class="casa-mls__head">
    {%- if s.kicker  != blank -%}<p class="casa-mls__mono">{{ s.kicker }}</p>{%- endif -%}
    {%- if s.heading != blank -%}<h2 class="casa-mls__h2">{{ s.heading }}</h2>{%- endif -%}
    {%- if s.lede    != blank -%}<p class="casa-mls__lede">{{ s.lede }}</p>{%- endif -%}
  </header>

  <div class="casa-mls__stage">
    <div class="casa-mls__modes" role="tablist">
      <button type="button" class="casa-mls__mode is-on" data-mls-mode="sync"  role="tab" aria-selected="true">
        <span class="casa-mls__mono">A</span>
        <span class="lab">{{ s.mode_a_label | default: 'Sync' }}</span>
        <span class="hint">{{ s.mode_a_hint | default: 'All same color' }}</span>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="casa-mls__mode" data-mls-mode="zone" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
        <span class="casa-mls__mono">B</span>
        <span class="lab">{{ s.mode_b_label | default: 'Zone' }}</span>
        <span class="hint">{{ s.mode_b_hint | default: 'Each room its own mood' }}</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="casa-mls__rooms">
      {%- for block in room_blocks -%}
        {%- assign b = block.settings -%}
        <div class="casa-mls__room" data-mls-room data-room-offset="{{ forloop.index0 }}" data-lamp-shape="{{ s.lamp_shape | default: 'apollo' }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <div class="casa-mls__room-glow" data-mls-glow></div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Apōllō silhouette — traced from the official product line drawing.
            One slim vertical pole (FLAT top — the real product cap is flat,
            not rounded; the RGB diffuser channel runs all the way to the top
            edge) + two splayed legs forming a tripod base. Leg span ~75% of
            viewBox width; legs angled ~28° below horizontal.

            PHYSICS NOTE — this is critical and the merchant flagged it:
            the entire visible body of the lamp (pole + legs) is matte black
            aluminium. The LED diffuser is on the BACK of the pole, projecting
            light onto the corner walls behind. From a face-on view we see:
              - matte black silhouette (pole + legs) in front
              - colored wall-wash behind, on the corner walls
              - subtle scene-color rim along the pole's vertical edges where
                the back-diffuser light wraps around the aluminium extrusion
            We do NOT paint the pole's front face with the scene color — that
            would imply the LED faces forward, which it doesn't.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 280 468" class="casa-mls__lamp" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax meet" aria-hidden="true">
            <defs>
              {%- comment -%}
                Two SVG filters only:
                - rim blur: soft halo on the lit pole edges
                - floor blur: smears the contact shadow into a
                  diffuse smudge under the legs so it never reads
                  as a distinct floating shape
                The earlier wall-wash filter + linearGradient are
                gone — the room glow div (a CSS radial behind the
                SVG) is the ONLY emission system now. Single
                gradient = no "bars / banding" between layers.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <filter id="mls-blur-rim-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }}" x="-300%" y="-5%" width="700%" height="110%">
                <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="1.5" />
              </filter>
              <filter id="mls-blur-floor-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }}" x="-50%" y="-100%" width="200%" height="300%">
                <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="6" />
              </filter>
              {%- comment -%}
                Wide bloom filter for the infinity-floor diffuser's
                outer aura layer. stdDeviation=6 keeps the visible
                blur extent within ~12px of the bloom rect bounds —
                small enough that the bloom stays inside the SVG
                viewBox + panel overflow:hidden bounds without an
                abrupt cutoff line at the top of the loop.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <filter id="mls-blur-glow-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }}" x="-200%" y="-5%" width="500%" height="110%">
                <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="6" />
              </filter>
            </defs>

            {%- comment -%}
              Per-product silhouette geometry. Apollo (default) is the
              V-shape pole-on-two-legs tripod. Nova is a slim column on
              a round base disc — same RGB physics (back-diffuser pole,
              edge rims wrap) but no splayed legs. Add new shapes as
              the floor-lamp family ports continue.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- case s.lamp_shape | default: 'apollo' -%}

            {%- when 'nova' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              NOVA silhouette — proportions derived from the spec sheet
              (Scene_30 measurement diagram):
                pole 147 cm × base 25 cm        → ratio 17%
                pole diameter ~2.5 cm           → ratio 1.7%

              In viewBox 280×468 with pole running y=6 → y=440
              (height 434):
                base radius  = 434 × 0.17 ≈ 37px  (rx=37)
                pole width   = 434 × 0.017 ≈ 7px  (x=136.5 .. x=143.5)
                floor shadow ≈ 50px (slightly wider than the disc)

              PHYSICS — same as Apollo: front face matte black, LED
              diffuser on the BACK projects wall-wash on the corner
              wall behind. Edge rims wrap the LEFT and RIGHT edges
              where the back-diffuser light bleeds around the
              extrusion. The pole's center 4px (x=138.5 .. x=142.5)
              stays unrimmed dark so the silhouette reads against
              the bright wall behind.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- comment -%} Floor shadow — tight under the small disc {%- endcomment -%}
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="464" rx="50" ry="2.8"
                     fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.45)"
                     filter="url(#mls-blur-floor-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- comment -%} Base — small round disc, slight perspective elevation {%- endcomment -%}
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="444" rx="37" ry="4.5" fill="#050508" />
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="440" rx="37" ry="4.5" fill="#15151B"
                     stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.18)" stroke-width="0.5" />
            <path d="M 103 440 L 103 444" fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.22)" stroke-width="0.4" />
            <path d="M 177 440 L 177 444" fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.22)" stroke-width="0.4" />

            {%- comment -%}
              POLE — 7px wide matte black aluminium column, flat top.
              x=136.5 .. x=143.5. Bottom (y=440) meets new disc top.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <path d="M 136.5 6 L 143.5 6 L 143.5 440 L 136.5 440 Z"
                  fill="#15151B"
                  stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.32)" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-linejoin="round" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Edge rims — back-diffuser wrap on the LEFT and RIGHT
              edges only. 2px wide each, overlapping the pole edges
              by 1px. Run from y=6 to y=434 (stop 6px short of disc
              top so rim doesn't bleed onto disc face). Pole's
              center 4px stays unrimmed.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="135.5" y="6" width="2" height="428" fill="currentColor" data-mls-rim
                  filter="url(#mls-blur-rim-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" opacity="1" />
            <rect x="142.5" y="6" width="2" height="428" fill="currentColor" data-mls-rim
                  filter="url(#mls-blur-rim-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" opacity="1" />

            {%- when 'genix' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              GENIX silhouette — twin-helix on a central black aluminum spine.
              Proportions from sizing metafield (135 cm tall × 25 cm base):
                in viewBox 280×468 with pole height 434:
                  base radius = 434 × 0.185 ≈ 40px
                  spine width 4px central black bar
                  helix envelope swings x=140 ± 30 (110 to 170)
                  cross-overs at y=110, 200, 290, 380 → 4 visible rungs
                  4 horizontal black "rungs" along the spine (visible in
                  product photos — the aluminum frame's structural cross-bars)

              PHYSICS: unlike Apollo/Nova where the LED is back-only and
              edges glow, Genix's helix IS the light source — full-
              circumference LED extrusion wrapping each helical curve.
              The two helix paths render in currentColor (cycle with
              scene) with rim blur for the wall-wash glow.
            {%- endcomment -%}

            {%- comment -%} Floor shadow — tight under the small base {%- endcomment -%}
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="464" rx="55" ry="3"
                     fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.45)"
                     filter="url(#mls-blur-floor-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- comment -%} Base disc — small round, proportional to 25cm/135cm ratio {%- endcomment -%}
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="444" rx="40" ry="5" fill="#050508" />
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="440" rx="40" ry="5" fill="#15151B"
                     stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.18)" stroke-width="0.5" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Helix 1 — right-leaning twist starting at top. Cubic-bezier
              approximation of a sine wave, amplitude 30, wavelength 180,
              4 visible cross-overs at y=110/200/290/380.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <path d="M 140 6 C 175 30, 175 80, 140 110 C 105 140, 105 180, 140 200 C 175 220, 175 270, 140 290 C 105 310, 105 360, 140 380 L 140 440"
                  fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"
                  data-mls-rim filter="url(#mls-blur-rim-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- comment -%} Helix 2 — left-leaning twist, phase-shifted to cross helix 1 {%- endcomment -%}
            <path d="M 140 6 C 105 30, 105 80, 140 110 C 175 140, 175 180, 140 200 C 105 220, 105 270, 140 290 C 175 310, 175 360, 140 380 L 140 440"
                  fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"
                  data-mls-rim filter="url(#mls-blur-rim-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- comment -%} Central spine — slim black aluminum bar, runs full height behind the helices {%- endcomment -%}
            <path d="M 138 6 L 142 6 L 142 440 L 138 440 Z"
                  fill="#15151B"
                  stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.32)" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-linejoin="round" />

            {%- comment -%} 4 horizontal rungs at the helix cross-over points {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="118" y="109" width="44" height="2" fill="#15151B" />
            <rect x="118" y="199" width="44" height="2" fill="#15151B" />
            <rect x="118" y="289" width="44" height="2" fill="#15151B" />
            <rect x="118" y="379" width="44" height="2" fill="#15151B" />

            {%- when 'infinity-floor' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              INFINITY FLOOR silhouette — tall narrow pill loop on a
              thin stem + small round base disc.

              PRODUCT MODEL (from dim diagram + lit product photos):
                · 140 cm tall total · 12 cm wide loop · 18 cm base disc
                · Loop = matte black aluminium frame, pill shape
                · LED diffuser is RECESSED inside the frame channel,
                  facing INWARD into the loop's open center
                · You do NOT see the diffuser as a visible bright strip
                  — what photos catch as a "bright line" is the LIGHT
                  RADIATING around the frame, not a visible component
                · Loop interior is HOLLOW — viewer sees through to wall
                · Wall behind picks up a SMOOTH organic color reflection
                  from the inner diffuser bouncing light, not a centered
                  hard radial peak (handled in the JS room-glow branch)

              In viewBox 280×468 (effective height ~434):
                loop body: x=121-159 (38 px wide), y=6-394 (388 px tall)
                stem: 3 px wide y=394-414
                base: ellipse rx=28 ry=4 at cy=414
            {%- endcomment -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Floor shadow — sized for the smaller base disc.
              rx=45 (was 55) matches the new disc spread.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="458" rx="45" ry="2.5"
                     fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.45)"
                     filter="url(#mls-blur-floor-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Base disc — corrected per the dim diagram (base=18cm,
              loop=12cm → 1.5× ratio). Was 84px wide (way too
              large); now 60px wide (rx=30), matching the product
              photo proportions. ry=5 keeps it as a flat disc.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="430" rx="30" ry="5" fill="#050508" />
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="426" rx="30" ry="5" fill="#15151B"
                     stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.18)" stroke-width="0.5" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Stem — CONTINUOUS from the joint ball at the very
              bottom of the loop's interior (top at y=376, the
              ball's center) down to the top of the base disc
              (y=421). Stem's upper portion sits inside the loop
              at the very bottom of the U-curve, exits through
              the matte frame's bottom at y=380, continues down
              to the base.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="137.5" y="376" width="5" height="45" fill="#15151B" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Joint ball at the VERY BOTTOM of the loop's open
              interior, sitting at the U-curve's flattest point.
              cy=376 r=3.5 places the ball with its bottom edge
              right at the inner matte bottom curve (y=377-378),
              so the ball reads as "resting at the bottom of the
              loop" — matches the product photo where the ball
              sits at the lowest point of the loop's interior,
              not floating in the lower third.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <circle cx="140" cy="376" r="3.5" fill="#15151B"
                    stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.32)" stroke-width="0.4" />

            {%- comment -%}
              The CYLINDRICAL frame channel has visible THICKNESS —
              from the camera you see two parallel black outlines
              (outer edge + inner edge of the channel wall). Both
              painted in matte black aluminium. The LED diffuser
              lives on the INNER face of the channel, between the
              inner black outline and the loop's hollow center —
              visible as a thin cycling-color line glowing into
              the open middle. Nothing is filled.

              Outer body edge:    rect at rx=20, sw=1.5
              Inner body edge:    rect at rx=17, sw=1.5
              Diffuser strip:     rect at rx=15, sw=1.5 currentColor
                                  with rim-blur (the visible LED face)
            {%- endcomment -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Layer order (back to front):
              1. Wide bloom aura — large stroke OUTSIDE the matte
                 frame (rx=24), heavy blur. Spreads outward onto
                 the wall, NEVER inward into the loop's open
                 middle (wrong layer geometry was the previous
                 bug — bloom rect was at rx=15 INSIDE the frame,
                 so its blur filled the interior).
              2. Outer matte black edge — defines the visible
                 outer perimeter of the cylindrical frame.
              3. Inner matte black edge — creates the visible
                 channel thickness.
              4. Sharp diffuser line — currentColor stroke just
                 inside the inner black edge (rx=15). The visible
                 LED line itself; no blur, no fill.

              Result: bright glow radiating OUTWARD onto the wall,
              defined frame outline, sharp LED line on the inside
              face, hollow open middle untouched.
            {%- endcomment -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Loop body height is 365 (vs the prior 390) — the
              real product photo shows the loop at ~78-80% of the
              total lamp height (loop=125cm, total=140cm → 89%
              just for the loop, but visually with the base disc
              accounting for the bottom, the loop reads ~80%).
              Loop spans y=15 (top) to y=380 (bottom curve junction
              where it meets the joint ball at cy=383).
            {%- endcomment -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Layer 1 — wide bloom outside the matte frame.
              rx=24 (outside matte's rx=20), y=15 height=365,
              opacity 0.35, blur stdDev=6. Soft wall halo around
              the body without overpowering the black frame.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="116" y="15" width="48" height="365" rx="24" ry="24"
                  fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="10" opacity="0.35"
                  filter="url(#mls-blur-glow-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Layer 2 — outer matte black edge.
              sw=2.5 keeps the frame body visibly black against
              the bloom outside it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="120" y="15" width="40" height="365" rx="20" ry="20"
                  fill="none" stroke="#15151B" stroke-width="2.5" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Layer 3 — inner matte black edge.
              sw=2.5 + 3px geometric gap to the outer edge = a
              clearly visible matte black channel body (the
              cylindrical frame profile).
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="123" y="18" width="34" height="359" rx="17" ry="17"
                  fill="none" stroke="#15151B" stroke-width="2.5" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Layer 4 — sharp diffuser line (the visible LED).
              Just inside the inner black edge, currentColor stroke
              cascades from `lamp.style.color` (no data-mls-rim,
              no fill — the open middle stays transparent).
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="125" y="20" width="30" height="355" rx="15" ry="15"
                  fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" />

            {%- when 'halo' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              HALO silhouette — circular LED ring on aluminum tripod.
              Proportions from Scene_20 measurement diagram:
                ring 13 in / 33 cm  ·  tripod base 21 in / 55 cm  ·  height 59 in / 150 cm
              In viewBox 280×468 (1 cm ≈ 2.9 px on effective height 434):
                ring diameter 95 px → radius 47, centered cx=140 cy=75
                tripod base 160 px → legs to ±80 from center
                joint hub at (140, 125) where 3 legs meet the ring stem
              Physics: ring IS the light (full-circumference LED extrusion).
              Outer matte black frame + inner LED ring in currentColor.
            {%- endcomment -%}

            {%- comment -%} Floor shadow — wider, tracks tripod spread {%- endcomment -%}
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="464" rx="80" ry="3"
                     fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.4)"
                     filter="url(#mls-blur-floor-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- comment -%} Tripod legs — 3 thin black bars from joint hub to floor {%- endcomment -%}
            <line x1="140" y1="130" x2="60" y2="460" stroke="#15151B" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
            <line x1="140" y1="130" x2="140" y2="460" stroke="#15151B" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
            <line x1="140" y1="130" x2="220" y2="460" stroke="#15151B" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />

            {%- comment -%} Tripod joint hub — small block where legs meet ring stem {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="135" y="124" width="10" height="12" fill="#15151B"
                  stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.32)" stroke-width="0.5" />

            {%- comment -%} Side bracket arms — small mount detail on ring sides {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="88" y="71" width="6" height="8" fill="#15151B" />
            <rect x="186" y="71" width="6" height="8" fill="#15151B" />

            {%- comment -%} Ring outer — matte black aluminium frame {%- endcomment -%}
            <circle cx="140" cy="75" r="47"
                    fill="none" stroke="#15151B" stroke-width="4" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Inner LED ring — currentColor (cycles with scene),
              slight inset from outer frame, full 360° emission.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <circle cx="140" cy="75" r="42"
                    fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" data-mls-rim
                    filter="url(#mls-blur-rim-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- when 'helix' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              HELIX silhouette — gently S-twisted aluminum column on
              small flat square base.

              IMPORTANT: per Scene_31 measurement diagram, Helix is NOT
              a tight spiral coil. Product name refers to the slight
              helical twist of a single flat extrusion.

              Spec: column 130 cm tall × square base 15 cm wide.
              Helix is the SHORTEST lamp in the floor-lamp family
              (vs Apollo 158, Halo 150, Nova 140, Infinity 140, Genix
              135). The silhouette must read shorter than its siblings,
              so the column starts at y=90 (not y=6), giving ~80px of
              ceiling space above the lamp inside the viewBox.

              In viewBox 280×468 / floor anchor y=442:
                column height = 352px = (130/158) × 434, matching the
                relative-to-Apollo ratio
                column: S-curve from y=90 to y=442 (top to base)
                stroke widths: outer matte black sw=10, inner LED sw=4
                  (the earlier 6/2 was too thin to register as a visible
                  pole next to the bigger silhouettes of other lamps)
                base: flat square slab x=115-165 (50px wide), y=442-451
                floor shadow: rx=35
            {%- endcomment -%}

            {%- comment -%} Floor shadow — small, tracks the slim base {%- endcomment -%}
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="464" rx="35" ry="2.5"
                     fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.45)"
                     filter="url(#mls-blur-floor-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- comment -%} Base — flat square slab, slight perspective {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="115" y="448" width="50" height="3" fill="#050508" />
            <rect x="115" y="442" width="50" height="6" fill="#15151B"
                  stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.18)" stroke-width="0.5" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Column — gentle S-curve from y=90 (top) to y=442 (base).
              Two strokes: outer matte black aluminum sw=10 (thick
              enough to read as a real pole) + inner LED stripe in
              currentColor sw=4 (visible LED, rim-blurred for glow).
              Control points scaled from the full-height variant by
              0.807 (= 352/436) so the S-curve preserves its shape
              just compressed to the shorter span.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <path d="M 140 442 C 130 392, 152 311, 140 247 C 128 190, 152 134, 140 90"
                  fill="none" stroke="#15151B" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round" />
            <path d="M 140 442 C 130 392, 152 311, 140 247 C 128 190, 152 134, 140 90"
                  fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" data-mls-rim
                  filter="url(#mls-blur-rim-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Single soft floor shadow. Wider, flatter, and heavily
              blurred so it reads as "the floor near the legs is a
              touch darker", not as a separate ellipse object. The
              earlier two-ellipse stack rendered as a visible dark
              shape under the lamp — exactly the "floating shadow"
              the user kept flagging.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <ellipse cx="140" cy="464" rx="110" ry="4"
                     fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.45)"
                     filter="url(#mls-blur-floor-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Geometry — continuous Y-junction (no gap at the pole↔leg seam).
              Each leg's near-pole edge is set so its top stroke, when extended,
              passes exactly through the pole's matching bottom-side corner:

                pole bottom corners:  (137, 395) left   |   (143, 395) right
                LEFT  leg far-end:    (28,  451)
                RIGHT leg far-end:    (252, 451)
                slope ±0.513 → at x=137 (or x=143) top edge = 395.08

              Both legs cross UNDER the pole (LEFT extends to x=143, RIGHT
              extends to x=137); the pole renders on top and hides the overlap,
              so the only visible seam is the smooth meeting of leg top edges
              with the pole's bottom corners.
            {%- endcomment -%}

            {%- comment -%} LEFT LEG — top face + thin front face for depth {%- endcomment -%}
            <path d="M 143 392 L 28 451 L 28 455 L 143 396 Z" fill="#15151B" />
            <path d="M 143 396 L 28 455 L 28 459 L 143 400 Z" fill="#050508" />
            <path d="M 143 392 L 28 451" fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.32)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-linecap="round" />
            <path d="M 28 459 L 143 400" fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.08)" stroke-width="0.4" stroke-linecap="round" />

            {%- comment -%} RIGHT LEG — mirror {%- endcomment -%}
            <path d="M 137 392 L 252 451 L 252 455 L 137 396 Z" fill="#15151B" />
            <path d="M 137 396 L 252 455 L 252 459 L 137 400 Z" fill="#050508" />
            <path d="M 137 392 L 252 451" fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.32)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-linecap="round" />
            <path d="M 252 459 L 137 400" fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.08)" stroke-width="0.4" stroke-linecap="round" />

            {%- comment -%}
              POLE — solid matte black aluminium silhouette with a FLAT top
              edge (the actual product is not capped/rounded; the RGB diffuser
              channel runs to the very top). NO front diffuser, NO inner LED
              stripe — the front face stays black; the lit moment lives in the
              wall-wash behind and the edge rims.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <path d="M 137 6 L 143 6 L 143 395 L 137 395 Z"
                  fill="#15151B"
                  stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.32)" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-linejoin="round" />

            {%- comment -%}
              Edge rims — narrow strips along the left and right sides of the
              pole picking up scene color (the back-diffuser light wrapping
              around the aluminium extrusion edges). Run from the very top of
              the pole down to the leg seam so the lit edge is unbroken.
              Soft-blurred so they read as a photographic light wrap, not a
              paint stripe on the pole.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <rect x="135.5" y="6" width="2" height="389" fill="currentColor" data-mls-rim
                  filter="url(#mls-blur-rim-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" opacity="1" />
            <rect x="142.5" y="6" width="2" height="389" fill="currentColor" data-mls-rim
                  filter="url(#mls-blur-rim-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }})" opacity="1" />

            {%- comment -%}
              NOTE: legs are pure matte black aluminium with NO RGB rim — the
              LED diffuser only lives in the pole, so only the pole's edges
              wrap with scene color. The legs sit in the wall-wash glow but
              don't carry color of their own (merchant-confirmed physics).
            {%- endcomment -%}

            {%- endcase -%}
          </svg>

          <div class="casa-mls__room-label">
            <span class="casa-mls__mono">{{ b.room_name | default: 'Room' }}</span>
            <span class="scene" data-mls-scene>—</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- if strip_blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="casa-mls__strip">
        {%- for block in strip_blocks -%}
          {%- assign b = block.settings -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Glue NBSP around any " — " in the body so the em-dash never
            starts or ends a line on its own. CSS text-wrap: balance
            does most of the orphan-prevention work, but the em-dash
            is a special character the merchant explicitly chose as a
            typographic pause — keeping it tied to its neighbour words
            is a non-negotiable typographic rule that CSS alone can't
            enforce reliably across browsers.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign body_text = b.body | replace: ' — ', '&nbsp;—&nbsp;' -%}
          <div class="casa-mls__strip-item" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {%- if b.kicker != blank -%}<p class="casa-mls__mono">{{ b.kicker }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if b.body   != blank -%}<p>{{ body_text }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
/* Registered <color> custom property — UNLIKE a plain custom property
   (or a gradient, which is a non-animatable background-image), a
   registered color CAN be transitioned. One property drives the whole
   lamp: wall-wash glow, column edge-rims (currentColor), and the scene
   label. When JS retargets it, all of them cross-fade through vivid
   intermediate hues in unison instead of the old hard cut. Browsers
   without @property + relative-color fall back to the discrete swap
   (JS modern-path detect + the @supports blocks below). */
@property --mls-c {
  syntax: '<color>';
  inherits: true;
  initial-value: #F2FFA0;
}
.casa-mls {
  background: var(--mls-ink);
  color: var(--mls-paper);
  padding: var(--mls-pt) 0 var(--mls-pb);
  font-family: var(--font-body--family);
  /* Sticky add-to-cart bar height — matches casa-color-scene-player's
     --csp-bar-offset. Subtracted from svh so the section bottom never
     hides behind the bar at one-frame fit. */
  --mls-bar-offset: 96px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* One-frame fit — compress vertical rhythm so the section is close
   to one viewport tall on a typical laptop without LOCKING the
   section to viewport height. Locking caused two problems:
     (1) On mobile portrait the section padded itself to 100svh,
         leaving a wasted dark gap between section 4 and section 5.
     (2) Flex-filling the rooms grid squashed the lamp SVG panels
         into wide-short tiles, shrinking the lamp silhouettes.
   Now the section sizes to content; aggressive typography
   compression + sane room clamp keep total height close to one
   viewport without artificially padding to viewport. */
@media (min-width: 641px) and (min-height: 641px) {
  .casa-mls {
    padding: clamp(16px, 3.5vh, 40px) 0;
  }
}
.casa-mls__head {
  max-width: 1400px;
  margin: 0 auto 16px;
  padding: 0 clamp(20px, 5vw, 64px);
  /* Left-aligned editorial composition — matches stats-grid /
     scene-player / moods / faq so every section header on the
     PDP shares the same alignment (2026-05-15).
     Note: head goes full-width (no max-width, no auto margin) at
     desktop ≥1025px only — see the @media block below the 1700px
     room-label rule. 2026-05-16 scoping fix. */
  text-align: left;
}
.casa-mls__mono {
  /* Base mono — neutral defaults. Sub-context monos (mode toggles,
     room labels, strip items, block kickers) override color and
     letter-spacing per their context below. The SECTION HEAD kicker
     is brand-quiet via the `.casa-mls__head .casa-mls__mono` rule
     so only the head gets opacity 0.5 — sub-contexts stay full
     opacity. */
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: inherit;
  margin: 0 0 16px;
}
/* Brand-default quiet section-head kicker (cross-section unify pass,
   brand book §03 .section .kicker). The mono number is chrome, not a
   moment register. Brand color expression lives in the H2 italic-em
   trinity accent, one per heading. */
.casa-mls__head .casa-mls__mono { opacity: 0.5; }
.casa-mls__h2 {
  /* Brand-locked PDP H2 — uses the casa-pdp-h2-* tokens so this
     heading matches stats-grid / faq / csp / am editorial scale.
     2026-05-15: bumped from clamp(28,3.2vw,44) / 300 to the brand
     token spec (clamp(36,4.5vw,56) / 600) for cross-section
     header consistency. */
  font-family:    var(--casa-pdp-h2-family);
  font-size:      var(--casa-pdp-h2-size);
  font-weight:    var(--casa-pdp-h2-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--casa-pdp-h2-tracking);
  line-height:    var(--casa-pdp-h2-line);
  /* 14 → 6 per merchant: lift the grey lede up against the
     heading so the editorial header reads as one compact block,
     not heading + air + paragraph. Per-breakpoint overrides
     below tighten further on narrow viewports. */
  margin: 0 0 6px;
  color: var(--mls-paper);
  text-wrap: balance;
}
.casa-mls__h2 em {
  /* Inline em — the heading reads as one line on viewports that
     can fit "Pair one. Pair ten. One remote." (~iPad and above).
     At ≥1025px we force `white-space: nowrap` on the H2 below so
     the whole headline is GUARANTEED to sit on one line. Below
     1025px text-wrap: balance handles the natural break before
     the em ("Pair one. Pair ten." / "One remote."). */
  display: inline;
  font-style: italic;
  /* Brand book v1 §08: cap section-heading em weight at 600. */
  font-weight: 600;
  /* Gradient accent reads larger than surrounding text — merchant
     directive 2026-05-15 (brand book emphasis register). */
  font-size: 1.25em;
  /* Brand-trinity gradient: purple → pink → cyan. Matches
     --grad-text from the brand book (docs/brand-book-v1.html).
     Earlier draft was only 2 stops (pink → cyan), missing the
     purple anchor on the left.
     background-image (longhand) — NOT the `background` shorthand —
     so the shorthand can't silently reset background-clip later
     in the cascade. (casa-brand-tokens skill, Bug 1.) */
  background-image: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--mls-purple), var(--mls-pink), var(--mls-cyan));
  -webkit-background-clip: text;
          background-clip: text;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
  color: transparent;
}
.casa-mls__lede {
  font-size: clamp(14px, 1.5vw, 17px);
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
  max-width: 56ch;
  /* Base (<1025px): head is `text-align: left` and the H2 starts at
     the head's left padding edge. The lede MUST also be flush-left
     so its first character lines up vertically with the H2's first
     character — using `margin: 0` keeps the constrained 56ch block
     at the head's left edge instead of auto-centering it (which
     would shift the lede text ~190px right of the H2 at tablet
     widths). Desktop ≥1025px re-enables `margin: 0 auto` so the
     constrained block centers under the now-centered H2 — see the
     @media block at the bottom of this stylesheet. */
  margin: 0;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

.casa-mls__stage {
  display: grid;
  gap: clamp(12px, 1.8vh, 20px);
  padding: 0 clamp(20px, 5vw, 64px);
}

/* Ultrawide guardrail: the stage has no width cap, so the 3-up rooms grid
   renders 1092px-wide room cards at 3440px (measured live 2026-07-12).
   Cap at the global content ceiling — the head above is already 1400px
   centered at desktop, so alignment holds. No effect ≤1920px. */
@media (min-width: 1920px) {
  .casa-mls__stage {
    max-width: var(--casa-content-max-w, 1920px);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
}
.casa-mls__modes {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 12px;
  max-width: 560px;
  /* Center the toggle row inside the stage so it aligns with the
     centered head above. */
  margin: 0 auto;
}
.casa-mls__mode {
  text-align: left;
  background: #16161B;
  border: 1px solid #1F1F25;
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 16px 20px;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
  grid-template-rows: auto auto;
  column-gap: 14px;
  align-items: baseline;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
  color: var(--mls-paper);
}
.casa-mls__mode:hover { border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2); }
.casa-mls__mode.is-on {
  background: var(--mls-ink);
  border-color: var(--mls-cyan);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--mls-cyan), 0 0 0 4px rgba(242, 255, 160, 0.12);
}
.casa-mls__mode .casa-mls__mono {
  grid-row: 1 / 3;
  font-size: 14px;
  color: var(--mls-paper);
  width: 28px;
  height: 28px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
  border-radius: 50%;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  letter-spacing: 0;
  margin: 0;
}
.casa-mls__mode.is-on .casa-mls__mono {
  background: var(--mls-cyan);
  border-color: var(--mls-cyan);
  color: var(--mls-ink);
}
.casa-mls__mode .lab {
  font-size: 16px;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--mls-paper);
  letter-spacing: -0.005em;
}
.casa-mls__mode .hint {
  font-size: 12px;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

.casa-mls__rooms {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 12px;
  /* No outer frame — earlier draft wrapped the 3 rooms in a darker
     padded container with a top-to-bottom gradient + border. That
     created a faint horizontal band at the top of each card where
     the gradient lifted, reading as "cut off / blurred edge".
     Removing the frame lets the 3 cards sit side-by-side as
     standalone panels with their own rounded backgrounds — they
     flow into one another visually with just the gap between. */
  padding: 0;
  background: transparent;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 0;
  position: relative;
}
.casa-mls__room {
  position: relative;
  /* Per-room scene color (each room can differ in ZONE mode). Seeded
     to the first cycle hue; JS retargets it every tick and the
     transition below morphs the whole lamp there. --mls-fade is set
     from cycleMs in JS (~0.75× the dwell) for a continuous flowing
     feel; the 700ms here is the SSR fallback before JS paints. */
  --mls-c: var(--mls-cyan, #F2FFA0);
  transition: --mls-c var(--mls-fade, 700ms) ease-in-out;
  /* Fixed clamp — lamp SVG (viewBox 280×500, 1:1.79 portrait) gets
     enough room to render the full silhouette dramatically. Bigger
     than the previous clamp(320, 38vh, 480) because the merchant
     said the lamps were rendering "very tiny"; the lamp is the
     section's centerpiece and needs visual weight. dvh tracks iOS
     Safari's dynamic toolbar; vh is the fallback. */
  height: clamp(360px, 44vh, 540px);
  height: clamp(360px, 44dvh, 540px);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: flex-end;
  padding: 0;
  border-radius: 14px;
  overflow: hidden;
  /* Single smooth linear gradient — TOP starts at section ink so
     the rounded top corners blend invisibly into the section
     background (no visible cut-off edge). Brightens subtly down
     the panel to suggest a floor plane. NO overlay radials here —
     the room-glow div is the ONLY emission system, so there's no
     "bars / banding" between competing gradients. */
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--mls-ink) 0%, #121218 60%, #16161D 100%);
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  /* The cycle interval is already skipped under reduced motion; this
     also snaps the color on the one remaining trigger (Sync/Zone switch). */
  .casa-mls__room { transition: none; }
}
/* First-paint guard: JS holds this attribute across the initial color
   set, then drops it after a reflow. Without it a template whose first
   scene isn't the cyan seed would sweep cyan → scene-0 on hydration. */
.casa-mls[data-mls-warmup] .casa-mls__room { transition: none; }
.casa-mls__room-glow {
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  /* Legacy path only: JS swaps the whole gradient string, and this
     tries (in vain — background-image is discrete) to soften it. In
     the modern path below JS never touches this inline, and the
     wall-wash color comes from the animating --mls-c instead. */
  transition: background 0.5s ease;
}
/* Modern path — the wall-wash gradient is authored ONCE here with the
   scene color pulled live from --mls-c via relative-color syntax, so it
   recomputes (and smoothly interpolates) every frame the property
   animates. Gated on relative-color support, which the JS modern-path
   detect mirrors exactly, so JS only sets --mls-c here and never writes
   an inline background that would shadow these rules. */
@supports (color: rgb(from white r g b / 1)) {
  /* DEFAULT (apollo/nova/halo/helix/genix) — one strong centered
     wall-wash; the solid body masks the peak so the viewer sees the
     glow around it. Alphas match the legacy D0/99/66/3A/18 stops. */
  .casa-mls__room-glow {
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 100% at 50% 47%,
      rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.816) 0%,
      rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.6)   12%,
      rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.4)   25%,
      rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.227) 45%,
      rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.094) 70%,
      transparent 95%);
  }
  /* INFINITY-FLOOR — hollow loop, diffuser inside the channel: two
     bright radials flanking the frame + a wide low ambient wash, so
     the open middle stays near-ambient. Alphas match A0/70/40/1A +
     28/14 legacy stops. */
  .casa-mls__room[data-lamp-shape="infinity-floor"] .casa-mls__room-glow {
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 30% 85% at 41% 47%, rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.627) 0%, rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.439) 20%, rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.251) 45%, rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.102) 70%, transparent 95%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 30% 85% at 59% 47%, rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.627) 0%, rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.439) 20%, rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.251) 45%, rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.102) 70%, transparent 95%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 95% at 50% 47%, rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.157) 0%, rgb(from var(--mls-c) r g b / 0.078) 50%, transparent 90%);
  }
}
.casa-mls__lamp {
  position: absolute;
  left: 50%;
  /* Edge-rims are fill/stroke="currentColor"; driving color from the
     animating --mls-c makes them cross-fade in lockstep with the
     wall-wash. Legacy JS overrides this inline (hard cut, as before). */
  color: var(--mls-c);
  /* Anchored to the panel floor (bottom: 0) so the lamp's tripod
     contact shadow sits at the actual bottom of the panel rather
     than floating ~30-90px above it. The SVG uses
     preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax meet" which bottom-aligns the
     viewBox to the container — combined with the floor-ellipse
     fix above (cy 486 → 464), the lamp now reads as standing on
     the floor of the room. */
  bottom: 0;
  transform: translateX(-50%);
  width: 92%;
  max-width: 340px;
  height: 92%;
  /* overflow: visible — the infinity-floor's bloom layer (sw=10 +
     blur stdDev=6) extends a few pixels ABOVE y=0 in the viewBox.
     Default SVG overflow is hidden, which produced an abrupt
     horizontal cutoff line where the bloom met the viewBox top.
     Visible overflow lets the bloom fade naturally beyond the
     viewBox into the surrounding panel space. Other lamp
     silhouettes don't draw above y=0 so this is a no-op for
     them. */
  overflow: visible;
  /* Single black drop-shadow for depth — the lamp casts a real
     shadow onto the panel floor. The SVG's own wall-wash + edge
     rims provide all the colored glow; stacking colored
     drop-shadow filters on top fattened the silhouette into a
     wide cyan blob and read as a saturated blur, not a slim
     bright RGB column. Slim column wins over wide halo. */
  filter: drop-shadow(0 14px 28px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7));
  z-index: 1;
}
.casa-mls__room-label {
  position: absolute;
  left: 16px;
  bottom: 16px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 2px;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.casa-mls__room-label .casa-mls__mono { margin: 0; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55); }
.casa-mls__room-label .scene {
  font-family: var(--font-body--family);
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  text-transform: none;
  /* Modern path: color follows the animating --mls-c, so no element
     transition (that would lag it out of sync with the wall-wash). */
  color: var(--mls-c);
}
/* Legacy path only: JS sets the label color inline, so give it a
   local fade — the wall-wash can't fade there, but the label still can. */
@supports not (color: rgb(from white r g b / 1)) {
  .casa-mls__room-label .scene { transition: color 0.5s ease; }
}

.casa-mls__strip {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 12px;
  margin-top: 10px;
}
.casa-mls__strip-item {
  /* Minimal pill — kicker (cyan mono) on line 1, body (off-white)
     on line 2. Column flex everywhere keeps the 3-up grid aligned
     to the rooms above with title-on-top / text-below at every
     viewport. Padding is tight so the lamps remain the visual
     centerpiece and the pills stay accent-chrome. */
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 6px;
  border: 1px solid #1F1F25;
  background: #16161B;
  border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 12px 14px;
  min-width: 0;
}
.casa-mls__strip-item .casa-mls__mono {
  color: var(--mls-cyan);
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  white-space: nowrap;
  line-height: 1.4;
}
.casa-mls__strip-item p {
  font-size: 12px;
  line-height: 1.4;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
  margin: 0;
  min-width: 0;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* Mid-desktop panel-width fix. When the viewport falls below ~1700px the
   per-panel width drops under ~500px, at which point the lamp's tripod
   legs (which span ~152px from panel center at max-width 340px) reach
   the bottom-left corner where the room label sits. Move the label to
   top-left for any viewport below the threshold — only the narrow
   centered V-tip lives up there, so labels stay clear at every width.
   Above 1700px panels are wide enough that bottom-left labels read fine. */
@media (max-width: 1700px) {
  .casa-mls__room-label { top: 16px; left: 16px; bottom: auto; }
}

/* Desktop / laptop ≥1025px ONLY — all the merchant-requested
   fixes are gated here so mobile + tablet behavior is guaranteed
   unchanged.

   1. Head text + lede CENTER-aligned (2026-05-17 reversal — was
      left-flush from 2026-05-16). Head goes back to max-width
      1400 + margin auto so the constrained block sits centered
      on the viewport; text-align: center overrides the base
      left-align; lede uses margin auto to recenter the
      constrained-width paragraph within the head.
   2. H2 forced to one line via white-space:nowrap.
   3. Bottom strip kicker 11 → 13, body 12 → 15 so the strip
      reads at the same visual register as the lede on big
      screens. */
@media (min-width: 1025px) {
  .casa-mls__head {
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto 16px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .casa-mls__lede { margin: 0 auto; }
  .casa-mls__h2   { white-space: nowrap; }
  .casa-mls__strip-item .casa-mls__mono { font-size: 13px; }
  .casa-mls__strip-item p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5; }
}

/* 13" laptops (1280px and below).
   Caps the base h2 clamp(28, 3.6vw, 52) so it doesn't blow the
   one-frame budget on ~800px-tall laptops (after the 96px sticky
   add-to-cart bar). 32px max H2 here = ~75px of heading height
   on two lines — keeps total section ≤ ~680px. */
@media (max-width: 1280px) {
  .casa-mls__head { margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .casa-mls__mono { font-size: 11px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .casa-mls__h2 { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .casa-mls__lede { font-size: clamp(13px, 1.3vw, 15px); }
  .casa-mls__stage { gap: 12px; }
  .casa-mls__modes { gap: 10px; }
  .casa-mls__mode { padding: 12px 14px; }
  .casa-mls__rooms { gap: 10px; }
  .casa-mls__room  {
    height: clamp(320px, 42vh, 440px);
    height: clamp(320px, 42dvh, 440px);
  }
  .casa-mls__lamp  { max-width: 280px; }
}
/* iPad portrait / landscape (1024px and below). Strip stays 3-up
   (does NOT stack to 1-col) — three columns of small cards keep
   the section close to one frame on iPad. */
@media (max-width: 1024px) {
  .casa-mls__head { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .casa-mls__mono { font-size: 11px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .casa-mls__h2 { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  /* Lede visible on iPad/tablet — sized down so it doesn't crowd
     the rooms grid below. Was display:none in prior commits;
     merchant wants it back to match the rest of the Apollo PDP
     editorial rhythm (every section uses kicker + H2 + lede). */
  .casa-mls__lede { font-size: clamp(12px, 1.3vw, 14px); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .casa-mls__stage { gap: 10px; }
  .casa-mls__rooms { gap: 8px; }
  .casa-mls__room  {
    height: clamp(300px, 40vh, 400px);
    height: clamp(300px, 40dvh, 400px);
  }
  .casa-mls__lamp  { width: 95%; max-width: 240px; }
  /* Tighter label at iPad widths — panels can drop to ~200px wide on
     iPad mini portrait, where 11px BEDROOM would brush the V-tip. */
  .casa-mls__room-label { font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; top: 12px; left: 12px; }
  .casa-mls__room-label .scene { font-size: 12px; }
  .casa-mls__strip-item { padding: 10px 12px; gap: 5px; }
  .casa-mls__strip-item .casa-mls__mono { font-size: 10px; }
  .casa-mls__strip-item p { font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.35; }
}
/* Mobile portrait (≤640px wide). Section sizes to natural content
   height — NO min-height: 100svh, which was padding the section
   to full viewport height and leaving a wasted dark gap between
   sections 4 and 5. Flows seamlessly into section 5 (same Ink
   surface, no border). */
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .casa-mls { padding: 24px 0; }
  .casa-mls__head { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .casa-mls__mono { font-size: 11px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .casa-mls__h2 { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  /* Lede sized for phone portrait — 12.5px reads cleanly at 375px
     wide; max-width 100% so the merchant's 200-char paragraph
     uses the full panel width instead of the 56ch desktop cap. */
  .casa-mls__lede { font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 100%; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .casa-mls__modes { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 6px; max-width: none; }
  .casa-mls__mode { padding: 8px 10px; column-gap: 8px; border-radius: 10px; }
  .casa-mls__mode .casa-mls__mono { width: 22px; height: 22px; font-size: 11px; }
  .casa-mls__mode .lab { font-size: 13px; }
  .casa-mls__mode .hint { display: none; }
  .casa-mls__rooms { gap: 5px; }
  /* Mobile room height tuned to the lamp SVG's natural aspect
     (viewBox 280×468 ≈ 1:1.67). At iPhone SE 375px each panel is
     ~107px wide → ideal height ≈ 178px. Setting 180px keeps the
     panel from reading as a tall narrow rectangle (the 260px value
     in earlier commits gave 1:2.4 which the merchant flagged as
     "too extended"). Lamp width: 100% fills the panel; SVG
     preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax meet" keeps the silhouette
     anchored to the bottom even at the shorter height. */
  .casa-mls__room  { height: 180px; border-radius: 10px; }
  /* Lamp pulled down so the V-tip stays well below the label zone even
     on the narrowest Android (≈320px viewport → ≈87px panels). Lower
     bottom + shorter height = SVG content sits in the lower 60-70% of
     the panel, leaving a clear ~50px band at the top for the label. */
  .casa-mls__lamp  { width: 100%; max-width: none; bottom: 0; height: 92%; }
  /* Wall-wash kept ON at mobile — the merchant explicitly wants the
     RGB to read very bright, so the soft colored column behind the
     pole is part of that read. (Was hidden in a prior commit.) */
  /* Label moved to top-left (only the centered V-tip lives up there, so
     left-anchored labels stay clear). Reduced font + tighter spacing so
     "BEDROOM" doesn't reach panel center on tiny phones. */
  .casa-mls__room-label {
    left: 6px; top: 6px; bottom: auto;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .casa-mls__room-label .casa-mls__mono { font-size: 7.5px; margin: 0; }
  .casa-mls__room-label .scene { font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: -0.005em; }
  /* Mobile strip — 3-up under each lamp panel with single-line
     bodies. Required template body shortening to make this work
     (see commit "shorten strip bodies for 1-line 3-up mobile"):
     bodies are now 17/15/22 chars, fitting in ~95px of text area
     per card at iPhone SE 375px when padding + gap are tight.
     Tight padding (6px×8px), 9px kicker, 10px body land all three
     bodies on a single line per card while keeping the cards
     aligned beneath their corresponding lamp panels. */
  .casa-mls__strip {
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .casa-mls__strip-item {
    padding: 6px 8px;
    gap: 3px;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .casa-mls__strip-item .casa-mls__mono {
    font-size: 9px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  .casa-mls__strip-item p {
    font-size: 10px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
}

/* Phone (≤749px): keep "Pair one. Pair ten. One remote." on one line.
   Per merchant 2026-05-15: every Apollo PDP section heading reads as a
   single line on phones (it already does on tablet+desktop). Considered
   per-section divergence from brand-book v1 §03 H2 floor (28px) —
   applies only to viewports where the brand-spec floor visibly wraps. */
@media (max-width: 749px) {
  /* Floor lowered to 17px to absorb the 1.25em gradient-accent size
     bump on "Pair one. Pair ten. One remote." (31-char title) without
     wrapping at 375-430px phone widths. */
  .casa-mls__h2 { font-size: clamp(17px, 4.8vw, 28px); }
}

/* Landscape phones (e.g. 844×390). Width hits the 1024 breakpoint but
   height is way too short — tightens header + rooms so the section
   doesn't push tabs out of viewport.
   max-height-shorthand-justified: .casa-mls__head provides the side
   gutter via its own clamp(20px, 5vw, 64px) padding. Section root with
   0 side at this height is fine. */
@media (max-height: 500px) {
  .casa-mls { padding: 12px 0; }
  .casa-mls__head { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .casa-mls__mono { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .casa-mls__h2 { margin-bottom: 2px; }
  /* Landscape phones: lede stays visible but very compact —
     10.5px / 1.3 line-height keeps the 200-char paragraph
     within ~2 lines so it doesn't push the lamps + strip out
     of viewport on the 390-430px tall landscape phone. */
  .casa-mls__lede { font-size: 10.5px; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .casa-mls__stage { gap: 8px; }
  .casa-mls__rooms { gap: 6px; }
  .casa-mls__room  {
    height: clamp(140px, 38vh, 200px);
    height: clamp(140px, 38dvh, 200px);
  }
  .casa-mls__mode { padding: 6px 10px; }
  .casa-mls__mode .lab { font-size: 13px; }
}

{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
(function () {
  function init(root) {
    if (!root || root.dataset.mlsInit === '1') return;
    root.dataset.mlsInit = '1';

    var hexes = (root.dataset.cycleHexes || '').split('|').filter(Boolean);
    var names = (root.dataset.cycleNames || '').split('|');
    var totalScenes = hexes.length;
    if (totalScenes < 1) return;
    var cycleMs = parseInt(root.dataset.cycleMs, 10) || 1300;
    var mode = root.dataset.defaultMode === 'zone' ? 'zone' : 'sync';

    // Modern path: one animatable registered <color> (--mls-c) drives the
    // whole lamp, and CSS transitions the cross-fade. This detect MUST
    // mirror the stylesheet's @supports (relative-color) gate exactly, so
    // we never write an inline gradient that shadows the CSS one — nor
    // leave an unsupported browser with no wall-wash at all.
    var MORPH = !!(window.CSS && CSS.supports && CSS.supports('color', 'rgb(from white r g b / 1)'));
    // Fade ≈ 0.75× the dwell: colors flow almost continuously with a brief
    // settle. Clamped so very fast / slow cycle settings still read well.
    var fadeMs = Math.max(240, Math.min(1200, Math.round(cycleMs * 0.75)));
    root.style.setProperty('--mls-fade', fadeMs + 'ms');

    var rooms = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-mls-room]'));
    var modeBtns = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-mls-mode]'));
    var tick = 0;

    function paint() {
      rooms.forEach(function (room, i) {
        var offset = mode === 'sync' ? 0 : i;
        var idx = ((tick + offset) % totalScenes + totalScenes) % totalScenes;
        var hex = hexes[idx] || '#F2FFA0';

        // Modern path: retarget the one color property; CSS cross-fades
        // the wall-wash gradient, the currentColor edge-rims, and the
        // label color to `hex` together. Nothing else to write per tick.
        // (The label TEXT is handled separately in paintLabels so it can
        // snap at the fade midpoint instead of leading the color.)
        if (MORPH) {
          room.style.setProperty('--mls-c', hex);
          return;
        }

        // ── Legacy discrete path (pre-@property browsers) ──
        var sceneEl = room.querySelector('[data-mls-scene]');
        var glow = room.querySelector('[data-mls-glow]');
        var lampShape = room.dataset.lampShape || 'apollo';
        // Wall-wash radial — the ONLY background emission system in
        // the card. Configuration depends on lamp physics:
        //
        // DEFAULT (apollo, nova, halo, helix, genix) — back-diffuser
        // lamps where the LED sits on the back face of a SOLID body
        // in front of the wall. Strong centered radial, six-stop
        // smooth falloff. The lamp body blocks the brightest peak so
        // what the viewer sees is the wall-wash AROUND the body.
        //
        // INFINITY-FLOOR — the lamp is a hollow black pill frame
        // with the LED diffuser hidden INSIDE the frame channel,
        // facing inward. Light radiates around the frame in a soft
        // organic bounce, not as a strong centered peak behind a
        // solid body. Use a wider, dimmer, ultra-gradual ellipse so
        // the wall reflects color smoothly without ever reading as
        // a hard "filled" rectangle inside the loop's open middle.
        // Max alpha drops from D0(82%) to 50(31%) and the stops
        // taper across many intermediate values for a smooth wash.
        if (glow) {
          if (lampShape === 'infinity-floor') {
            // Loop is hollow + the diffuser sits inside the frame
            // channel. The wall behind the LOOP'S OPEN INTERIOR
            // must stay close to ambient (no centered radial peak
            // there — that would re-introduce the "filled middle"
            // look). But the wall AROUND the loop body should
            // glow brightly with the cycling color, because the
            // diffuser actually radiates in all directions and
            // the wall catches it.
            //
            // Three stacked gradients:
            //   1+2: two bright radials flanking the loop's vertical
            //        sides (41% / 59% horizontal) — peak alpha A0
            //        (62%) so the wall by the lamp glows
            //        distinctly. Wider 30%×85% than before so the
            //        bleed reaches floor + ceiling of the panel.
            //   3:   a wide low-alpha ambient wash centered on the
            //        whole panel (alpha 28 = 16%) — adds room-level
            //        color cast so the lamp feels like it's lighting
            //        the whole space, not just two stripes.
            // The two flanking radials fall off sharply at center
            // (50%), so the loop's open middle still reads
            // essentially as ambient, just gently tinted.
            glow.style.background =
              'radial-gradient(ellipse 30% 85% at 41% 47%, ' + hex + 'A0 0%, ' + hex + '70 20%, ' + hex + '40 45%, ' + hex + '1A 70%, transparent 95%), ' +
              'radial-gradient(ellipse 30% 85% at 59% 47%, ' + hex + 'A0 0%, ' + hex + '70 20%, ' + hex + '40 45%, ' + hex + '1A 70%, transparent 95%), ' +
              'radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 95% at 50% 47%, ' + hex + '28 0%, ' + hex + '14 50%, transparent 90%)';
          } else {
            glow.style.background =
              'radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 100% at 50% 47%, ' + hex + 'D0 0%, ' + hex + '99 12%, ' + hex + '66 25%, ' + hex + '3A 45%, ' + hex + '18 70%, transparent 95%)';
          }
        }

        var lit = room.querySelectorAll('[data-mls-halo], [data-mls-rim]');
        lit.forEach(function (el) { el.setAttribute('fill', hex); });

        // Set CSS color so any remaining `currentColor` references resolve to the scene hex
        var lamp = room.querySelector('.casa-mls__lamp');
        if (lamp) lamp.style.color = hex;

        if (sceneEl) sceneEl.style.color = hex;
      });
    }

    // Scene-label TEXT for the current tick. Kept out of paint() so the
    // word can snap at the color-fade MIDPOINT (see scheduleLabels) — at
    // the smooth fade duration the destination word would otherwise lead
    // the color by nearly a full cycle (very visible on the palette wrap).
    function paintLabels() {
      rooms.forEach(function (room, i) {
        var offset = mode === 'sync' ? 0 : i;
        var idx = ((tick + offset) % totalScenes + totalScenes) % totalScenes;
        var sceneEl = room.querySelector('[data-mls-scene]');
        if (sceneEl) sceneEl.textContent = names[idx] || 'Scene';
      });
    }
    // Modern: swap words half-way through the color fade so they track the
    // hue. Legacy hard-cuts, so update immediately in lockstep.
    function scheduleLabels() {
      if (root.__mlsLabelT) { clearTimeout(root.__mlsLabelT); root.__mlsLabelT = null; }
      if (MORPH) root.__mlsLabelT = setTimeout(paintLabels, Math.round(fadeMs * 0.5));
      else paintLabels();
    }

    function setMode(next) {
      mode = next;
      modeBtns.forEach(function (b) {
        var on = b.dataset.mlsMode === next;
        b.classList.toggle('is-on', on);
        b.setAttribute('aria-selected', on ? 'true' : 'false');
      });
      paint();
      paintLabels();
    }

    modeBtns.forEach(function (b) {
      b.addEventListener('click', function () { setMode(b.dataset.mlsMode); });
    });

    // Commit the first scene's colors WITHOUT a transition (warmup guard),
    // then a reflow, then re-enable fades — so the initial hydration snaps
    // to scene 0 instead of sweeping there from the cyan seed.
    root.dataset.mlsWarmup = '';
    paint();
    paintLabels();
    void root.offsetWidth;
    delete root.dataset.mlsWarmup;

    // Static first scene under reduced motion — the paint above renders
    // the initial state; skip the cycling interval entirely.
    if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
      return;
    }

    // Cycle scene every cycleMs — gated by IntersectionObserver so the
    // feGaussianBlur-filtered shapes aren't re-rastered while the
    // section is off-screen (each repaint forces a CPU filter pass).
    function startCycle() {
      if (root.__mlsCycleId) return;
      root.__mlsCycleId = setInterval(function () { tick = (tick + 1) % totalScenes; paint(); scheduleLabels(); }, cycleMs);
    }
    function stopCycle() {
      if (root.__mlsCycleId) { clearInterval(root.__mlsCycleId); root.__mlsCycleId = null; }
      if (root.__mlsLabelT) { clearTimeout(root.__mlsLabelT); root.__mlsLabelT = null; }
    }

    if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
      root.__mlsIO = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
        entries.forEach(function (entry) {
          if (entry.isIntersecting) startCycle(); else stopCycle();
        });
      }, { threshold: 0.15 });
      root.__mlsIO.observe(root);
    } else {
      startCycle();
    }
  }

  function teardown(root) {
    if (!root) return;
    if (root.__mlsCycleId) { clearInterval(root.__mlsCycleId); root.__mlsCycleId = null; }
    if (root.__mlsLabelT) { clearTimeout(root.__mlsLabelT); root.__mlsLabelT = null; }
    if (root.__mlsIO) { root.__mlsIO.disconnect(); root.__mlsIO = null; }
    delete root.dataset.mlsInit;
  }

  function bootAll() {
    document.querySelectorAll('.casa-mls').forEach(init);
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', bootAll);
  } else {
    bootAll();
  }
  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', function (ev) {
    if (ev.target) ev.target.querySelectorAll('.casa-mls').forEach(function (node) { teardown(node); init(node); });
  });
  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:unload', function (ev) {
    if (ev.target) ev.target.querySelectorAll('.casa-mls').forEach(teardown);
  });
})();
{% endjavascript %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Casa Multi-lamp Sync",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "casa-multi-lamp-sync-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Heading" },
    { "type": "text",     "id": "kicker",  "label": "Kicker (mono)", "default": "04 · WHAT MAKES IT APŌLLŌ" },
    { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading (use <em>word</em> for italic gradient accent)", "default": "Pair one. Pair ten. <em>One remote.</em>" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "lede",    "label": "Lede", "default": "Every Apōllō Floor Lamp pairs to the same remote. Sync them across rooms for a unified ambiance, or zone them to give each space its own mood — bedroom hush, dinner glow, party blaze." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Mode toggle labels" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mode_a_label", "label": "Mode A label", "default": "Sync"  },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mode_a_hint",  "label": "Mode A hint",  "default": "All same color" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mode_b_label", "label": "Mode B label", "default": "Zone" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mode_b_hint",  "label": "Mode B hint",  "default": "Each room its own mood" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "default_mode", "label": "Default mode", "default": "sync",
      "options": [
        { "value": "sync", "label": "Sync" },
        { "value": "zone", "label": "Zone" }
      ]
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Lamp silhouette geometry" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "lamp_shape", "label": "Lamp shape",
      "info": "Switches the SVG silhouette per product. Apollo = pole + two splayed legs. Nova = slim pole + round disc base.",
      "default": "apollo",
      "options": [
        { "value": "apollo", "label": "Apollo — pole + tripod legs" },
        { "value": "nova",   "label": "Nova — slim pole + round base" },
        { "value": "genix",  "label": "Genix — twin-helix on black aluminum spine" },
        { "value": "halo",  "label": "Halo — ring on tripod" },
        { "value": "helix", "label": "Helix — S-twist column on flat base" },
        { "value": "infinity-floor", "label": "Infinity Floor — pill loop on stem + disc" }
      ]
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Color cycle (up to 6 stops)" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Each glow rotates through these scenes. Order matters — in Zone mode the 3 rooms always show 3 CONSECUTIVE entries, so keep adjacent stops harmonious. Default cycle (Cyan→Sky→Indigo→Purple→Magenta→Pink) walks the brand spectrum so every triple stays brand-aligned." },
    { "type": "text",  "id": "scene_name_1", "label": "Scene 1 name", "default": "Cyan" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "scene_hex_1",  "label": "Scene 1 hex",  "default": "#F2FFA0" },
    { "type": "text",  "id": "scene_name_2", "label": "Scene 2 name", "default": "Sky" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "scene_hex_2",  "label": "Scene 2 hex",  "default": "#38BDF8" },
    { "type": "text",  "id": "scene_name_3", "label": "Scene 3 name", "default": "Indigo" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "scene_hex_3",  "label": "Scene 3 hex",  "default": "#6366F1" },
    { "type": "text",  "id": "scene_name_4", "label": "Scene 4 name", "default": "Purple" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "scene_hex_4",  "label": "Scene 4 hex",  "default": "#B0C3FA" },
    { "type": "text",  "id": "scene_name_5", "label": "Scene 5 name", "default": "Magenta" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "scene_hex_5",  "label": "Scene 5 hex",  "default": "#D946EF" },
    { "type": "text",  "id": "scene_name_6", "label": "Scene 6 name", "default": "Pink" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "scene_hex_6",  "label": "Scene 6 hex",  "default": "#5E0A02" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "cycle_ms", "label": "Cycle interval", "min": 600, "max": 6000, "step": 100, "default": 1300, "unit": "ms" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Colors" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "color_paper",  "label": "Paper",         "default": "#FAFAF7" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "color_ink",    "label": "Ink",           "default": "#0A0A0F" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "color_purple", "label": "Accent purple", "default": "#B0C3FA" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "color_pink",   "label": "Accent pink",   "default": "#5E0A02" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "color_cyan",   "label": "Accent cyan",   "default": "#F2FFA0" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Spacing" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_top",    "label": "Padding top",    "min": 0, "max": 160, "step": 4, "default": 96, "unit": "px" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_bottom", "label": "Padding bottom", "min": 0, "max": 160, "step": 4, "default": 96, "unit": "px" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "room",
      "name": "Room",
      "limit": 6,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "room_name", "label": "Room name (mono uppercase)", "default": "BEDROOM" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "strip",
      "name": "Bottom strip card",
